$ floe template check templates/c templates/m templates/w templates/y
exit 1
--- stderr
templates/c/checks.yaml:1:1: a key is a name: write 1 as text, in quotes
templates/c/checks.yaml:1:1: write checks.yaml as a list of checks, each with expr and message (and for and field if you like)
templates/m/computed.yaml:1:1: write computed.yaml as names and expressions, like total: sum(items, .price)
templates/m/computed.yaml:1:4: a key is a name: write 1 as text, in quotes
templates/w/words.yaml:1:1: write words.yaml as language tags, each the names of the words and their text
templates/w/words.yaml:1:4: a key is a name: write 1 as text, in quotes
templates/y/template.yaml:1:1: write template.yaml as one key, floe:, and the version of floe the template needs, like floe: 1.2
templates/y/template.yaml:1:4: a key is a name: write 1 as text, in quotes
the part p cannot be used
  $SAMPLE/parts/p/part.yaml:1:1: write part.yaml as keys and values: looks:, the list of the looks the part takes, like looks: [panel], and a look alone's description:
  $SAMPLE/parts/p/part.yaml:1:4: a key is a name: write 1 as text, in quotes
$ floe part check
exit 1
--- stderr
the part p cannot be used
  $SAMPLE/parts/p/part.yaml:1:1: write part.yaml as keys and values: looks:, the list of the looks the part takes, like looks: [panel], and a look alone's description:
  $SAMPLE/parts/p/part.yaml:1:4: a key is a name: write 1 as text, in quotes
$ floe diagram render diagrams/anchor.yaml diagrams/tag.yaml
exit 1
--- stderr
diagrams/anchor.yaml:1:1: anchors, aliases, merge keys (<<) and tags are not supported; write the value out
diagrams/anchor.yaml:1:4: diagram: write a mapping of keys and values
diagrams/tag.yaml:1:1: anchors, aliases, merge keys (<<) and tags are not supported; write the value out
diagrams/tag.yaml:1:6: diagram: write a mapping of keys and values
